---
/* L91 - repeats find the noise floor, and the floor decides what you can see. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L91.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of a laboratory bench with five test tubes in a rack, each holding a slightly different level of dark blue liquid, beside a ruler and a wavy trace."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L91-fig-title L91-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L91-fig-title">The noise floor decides which effects you can see</title>
      <desc id="L91-fig-desc">
        A horizontal scale of the size of a probability move. One bar, 0.10 long,
        reaches past the floor and is labelled visible. A second bar, 0.02 long, ends
        inside the floor and is labelled inside the floor. The floor itself is a
        bracket running from 0 to 0.05, labelled the noise floor 0.05, with a note
        that one provider's probabilities jitted by about 0.05 while another
        provider's repeats came back byte-identical. Below: three repeats, one raw
        line per call, 24 labelled cases as a small denominator, a spend cap of
        0.25 and a plan of 160 tokens per call.
      </desc>

      <text x="30" y="40" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" letter-spacing="0.09em" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">HOW FAR THE PROBABILITY MOVED</text>

      <!-- an effect that clears the floor -->
      <text x="30" y="116" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">effect 0.10</text>
      <g class="m-rise" style="--m-rise: 12px; --m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.5s;">
        <rect x="60" y="100" width="417" height="24" fill="var(--color-ink)" />
      </g>
      <text x="487" y="116" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">0.10</text>
      <text x="487" y="132" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">above the floor: visible</text>

      <!-- an effect that does not -->
      <text x="30" y="184" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">effect 0.02</text>
      <g class="m-rise" style="--m-rise: 12px; --m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.8s;">
        <rect x="60" y="168" width="83" height="24" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
      </g>
      <text x="153" y="180" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">0.02</text>
      <text x="153" y="196" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">inside the floor</text>

      <!-- the floor, drawn by the repeats -->
      <line x1="60" y1="219" x2="60" y2="233" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="268" y1="219" x2="268" y2="233" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <path
        class="m-draw"
        style="--m-length: 220; --m-duration: 1.2s;"
        d="M 60 226 H 268"
        fill="none"
        stroke="var(--color-ink-45)"
        stroke-width="1"
      />
      <text x="30" y="252" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">noise floor 0.05</text>
      <text x="30" y="268" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">one provider's probabilities jitted by about 0.05; another's repeats came back byte-identical</text>

      <!-- what else the run has to pin down -->
      <rect x="30" y="282" width="580" height="52" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="42" y="302" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">3 repeats: one raw line per call, so the jitter is in the file, not in your head</text>
      <text x="42" y="318" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">24 labelled cases is a small denominator: an observation, not a ranking</text>
      <text x="42" y="332" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">spend cap 0.25, on a plan of 160 tokens per call</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L91</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">Repeats measure the floor: on a provider that jitters by about 0.05, an effect of 0.10 is visible and an effect of 0.02 is not.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
